{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own","id":440056,"title":"Trigger warning: to each his own","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-13T09:54:44-07:00","id":440056,"title":"Trigger warning: to each his own","content":"I've got a question about death rage triggers that's a bit off topic from the other threads about death rage confusion I've found around.<br /> In the big, most-of-the-page splash about Kuruth triggers, it says something about everyone's triggers being different, and then it has triggers broken down into a bunch of categories followed by a small set of four (should be a couple more) &quot;General Triggers&quot;. <br /> Now, my main question is this: Does it say every is different because, at different Harmony you use passive, common, or specific triggers, or because everyone is supposed to pick a couple of those subheadings as THEIR triggers?<br /> For instance, is it fair to say that seeing a pack member get mauled is an issue for me, but human blood isn't, regarless of my Harmony or how much I guzzle?<br /> If it's the pick-and-choose latter option (which fits the &quot;everyone is different&quot; idea in the fluff), are there any guidelines for how many people should pick other than &quot;how often do you want to risk rage?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 03-13-2015, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:02:41-07:00","id":440085,"title":"","content":"This is answered in the text.<br /> <br /> Everyone is always susceptible to the 'General Triggers.' But after that you pick one specific, one common, and one passive trigger from the lists available, or make them yourself. There's a thread that has a few homebrewed triggers as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:20:03-07:00","id":440107,"title":"","content":"The text I'm going off of (again, WtF 2e page 103, in the Triggers box) says:<br /> &quot;Each werewolf has a set of Kuruth triggers that apply just to him. Which trigger affects him at any given time depends on his Harmony. A player should note down her character\u2019s passive, common, and specific triggers, so she knows what will affect her character when his Harmony changes.&quot;<br /> That doesn't sound to me like &quot;pick one of each&quot;. (Note, I'm not commenting on the General ones. Its clear that they apply to everyone, even perfectly harmony-balanced Uratha.)<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------<br /> As a side note, I'm new to forum usage and a little unclear on what's asked of us when citing specific texts from the book series this forum is dedicated to. Anyone have something they could point me to on that front, or is a moderator/employee around to say &quot;don't worry about it&quot; or &quot;don't copy text&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:48:23-07:00","id":440137,"title":"","content":"They should clear up the word usage but I believe it's been errata'd. You just pick one for each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:54:46-07:00","id":440142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=440107#post440107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note, I'm new to forum usage and a little unclear on what's asked of us when citing specific texts from the book series this forum is dedicated to. Anyone have something they could point me to on that front, or is a moderator/employee around to say &quot;don't worry about it&quot; or &quot;don't copy text&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can quote the books and cite the location found, just don't go posting up huge swathes of text straight from the book. Keep it short and relevant to the conversation at hand.<br /> <br /> A special addendum: If it's about Mummy and it pertains to the Storyteller section/Book of the Deceived, it is...well, polite to mark the thread/post you're making with a warning of/tags for spoilers. It's not longer mandated, but, you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T11:30:33-07:00","id":440192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=440142#post440142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A special addendum: If it's about Mummy and it pertains to the Storyteller section/Book of the Deceived, it is...well, polite to mark the thread/post you're making with a warning of/tags for spoilers. It's not longer mandated, but, you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having had zero exposure to Mummy, I'm not sure why you're speicifically calling it out as something subject to spoiler warnings. That said, I personally have kept my eyes out large sections of the Werewolf book to avoid spoilers as I'm not planning on playing Storyteller in my game, but have seen people making at least oblique references to those chapters here and there. Is there a good rule of thumb for where to post spoiler warnings other than that chapter/book of that line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:32:35-07:00","id":440300,"title":"","content":"Is the tittle to this thread a pun? Cuz I don't see no trigger stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:02:52-07:00","id":440380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=440300#post440300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the tittle to this thread a pun? Cuz I don't see no trigger stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah sorta. I wasn't meaning to actually warn anyone that this thread could cause death rage. I just wanted to talk about Kuruth triggers.<br /> <br /> The thread got a little off topic with the citations and the spoilers stuff, but my intial question was about Kuruth triggers and how they were supposed to be specific to each werewolf. I couldn't make out how you were supposed to choose a subset of all the triggers called out based on the text in the book.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping it gets cleared up in the final text, as I still don't read it as &quot;pick one of each type&quot;. It seems to me like you would pick the blood triggers or the moon triggers. Then, as your harmony gets out of whack, blood or the moon has an easier time triggering Kuruth for your character. On the other hand, someone else may have picked another section and neither blood or the moon ever has any effect on them, but the danger-to-pack triggers do.<br /> While I guess Kuruth is supposed to be kinda weird, it just seems... well, out there that at mild disharmony swallowing human blood would trigger rage, at moderate disharmony seeing a pack-mate attacked would also do it, but at wild disharmony your auspice moon could also trigger it. That seems so discongruous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:11:20-07:00","id":440387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=440380#post440380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah sorta. I wasn't meaning to actually warn anyone that this thread could cause death rage. I just wanted to talk about Kuruth triggers.<br /> <br /> The thread got a little off topic with the citations and the spoilers stuff, but my intial question was about Kuruth triggers and how they were supposed to be specific to each werewolf. I couldn't make out how you were supposed to choose a subset of all the triggers called out based on the text in the book.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping it gets cleared up in the final text, as I still don't read it as &amp;quot;pick one of each type&amp;quot;. It seems to me like you would pick the blood triggers or the moon triggers. Then, as your harmony gets out of whack, blood or the moon has an easier time triggering Kuruth for your character. On the other hand, someone else may have picked another section and neither blood or the moon ever has any effect on them, but the danger-to-pack triggers do.<br /> While I guess Kuruth is supposed to be kinda weird, it just seems... well, out there that at mild disharmony swallowing human blood would trigger rage, at moderate disharmony seeing a pack-mate attacked would also do it, but at wild disharmony your auspice moon could also trigger it. That seems so discongruous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Seems weird that a character who rages at the mere smell of human blood, but once their harmony balances out a bit, suddenly they don't care about human blood any more, but Wound Spirits really set them off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:25:01-07:00","id":440418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=440387#post440387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. Seems weird that a character who rages at the mere smell of human blood, but once their harmony balances out a bit, suddenly they don't care about human blood any more, but Wound Spirits really set them off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea is that if you're in the more out-of-balanced regimes, such that passive triggers could affect you, the common and specific ones would, too. So if they have it set up as nofather seems to be describing and you seem to be calling out, Charlaquin, then Wound Spirits would have been messing with that wolf the whole time. Its just the blood thing that would come back into check.<br /> What seems odd to me about your guy is that, while the initial interaction with wound-born would set him off, if he got through that and it attacked him, he might think no more of it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:36:14-07:00","id":440427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=440387#post440387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree. Seems weird that a character who rages at the mere smell of human blood, but once their harmony balances out a bit, suddenly they don't care about human blood any more, but Wound Spirits really set them off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Way I handle it, and how I understand it, you pick all the associated (passive, common, specific) triggers, and apply them depending on how your Harmony looks.<br /> <br /> Example 1: I'm at Harmony 5, my particular triggers don't apply.<br /> <br /> Example 2: I'm at Harmony 3-4 or 6-7, the specific triggers apply, let's say, Pack. I dramatically fail my firearms roll and injure a packmate, Wasu-Im.<br /> <br /> Example 3: I'm at Harmony 1-2 or 8-9, if (still having selected Pack as triggers) I see someone stabbing my Alpha, Bam! Wasu-Im.<br /> <br /> Example 4: I'm at Harmony 0 or 10. My beta breaks his arm in a domestic accident. Wasu-Im.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 03-13-2015, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:41:06-07:00","id":440435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=440192#post440192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having had zero exposure to Mummy, I'm not sure why you're speicifically calling it out as something subject to spoiler warnings. That said, I personally have kept my eyes out large sections of the Werewolf book to avoid spoilers as I'm not planning on playing Storyteller in my game, but have seen people making at least oblique references to those chapters here and there. Is there a good rule of thumb for where to post spoiler warnings other than that chapter/book of that line?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just an advance warning that has nothing to do with the conversation born out of an idle thought. I am an irrational man with chaotic thoughts.<br /> <br /> As for Werewolf, nah, the game doesn't really have spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:58:38-07:00","id":440443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=440427#post440427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Way I handle it, and how I understand it, you pick all the associated (passive, common, specific) triggers, and apply them depending on how your Harmony looks.<br /> <br /> Example 1: I'm at Harmony 5, my particular triggers don't apply.<br /> <br /> Example 2: I'm at Harmony 3-4 or 6-7, the specific triggers apply, let's say, Pack. I dramatically fail my firearms roll and injure a packmate, Wasu-Im.<br /> <br /> Example 3: I'm at Harmony 1-2 or 8-9, if (still having selected Pack as triggers) I see someone stabbing my Alpha, Bam! Wasu-Im.<br /> <br /> Example 4: I'm at Harmony 0 or 10. My beta breaks his arm in a domestic accident. Wasu-Im.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how I understand it as well. What I was saying wouldn't make sense is if you could select them individually, as it has been suggested by a few folks. As in one Passive from any list, one common from any list, and one specific from any list. It would be very strange if your character went from raging any time one of your packmates was injured at 0 or 10, to when you see a Vampire using blood sorcery at 1-2 or 8-9, to when you hear a wolf howl at your auspice moon at 3-4 or 6-7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:29:54-07:00","id":440522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own#post440056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, is it fair to say that seeing a pack member get mauled is an issue for me, but human blood isn't, regarless of my Harmony or how much I guzzle?<br /> If it's the pick-and-choose latter option (which fits the &quot;everyone is different&quot; idea in the fluff), are there any guidelines for how many people should pick other than &quot;how often do you want to risk rage?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone has to deal with <b>General Triggers</b>.<br /> You pick a single <b>Personal Trigger</b> for your character (Moon, The Other, Pack, etc).<br /> Your Harmony determines if you use the Passive, Common, or Specific Trigger within that category.<br /> <br /> The only thing that is unclear is whether or not you use one trigger (Specific OR Common OR Passive) or if you use all triggers (Specific AND Common AND Passive) when you have High / Low Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T16:17:51-07:00","id":440554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=440522#post440522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everyone has to deal with <b>General Triggers</b>.<br /> You pick a single <b>Personal Trigger</b> for your character (Moon, The Other, Pack, etc).<br /> Your Harmony determines if you use the Passive, Common, or Specific Trigger within that category.<br /> <br /> The only thing that is unclear is whether or not you use one trigger (Specific OR Common OR Passive) or if you use all triggers (Specific AND Common AND Passive) when you have High / Low Harmony.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like it makes little difference either way. You'd be hard pressed to swallow blood without also tasting and smelling it. If you cause lethal damage to one of your packmates, they are clearly taking lethal damage, and you are clearly witnessing it. Most of the triggers overlap enough at different levels, with just a few exceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T17:11:38-07:00","id":440647,"title":"","content":"I would say that if you had, say, the Common Trigger for Moon and your Specific Trigger for Moon got pulled you would still enter Wasu-Im. So that's how it makes sense to me. You are affected by the level of Trigger you Harmony leaves you open to in addition to the more specific ones. This way it isn't this absurd transition, and more just an addition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T20:58:48-07:00","id":440837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=440554#post440554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it makes little difference either way. You'd be hard pressed to swallow blood without also tasting and smelling it. If you cause lethal damage to one of your packmates, they are clearly taking lethal damage, and you are clearly witnessing it. Most of the triggers overlap enough at different levels, with just a few exceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood is the only one where it rarely makes a difference. All the others have some pretty notable examples where the difference becomes important:<br /> <br /> <b>Moon:</b> You are at the Common Trigger, but you hear a werewolf howl during your auspice moon?<br /> <b>The Other:</b> You are at the Common Trigger, but you are attacked by a supernatural power from an unknown location and distance?<br /> <b>Pack:</b> You are at the Common Trigger, but a werewolf outside of your territory challenges your packs ability to do its duty?<br /> <b>Wounds:</b> You are at the Common Trigger, but you are being attacked by a wound-born spirit?<br /> <br /> I just picked Common Trigger examples because Passive is fairly rare. I'm inclined to believe High / Low Harmony uses ALL applicable triggers, since that would make the most amount of sense. There's just nothing written to support or undermine it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T02:37:31-07:00","id":441120,"title":"","content":"Passive triggers are supposed to be rare and unavoidable. Your auspice moon is up. It doesn't matter if you're in a submarine underneath the ocean, the moon is up and you're going to death rage. Because you're very much unbalanced.<br /> <br /> Specific triggers are because you are mostly keeping it together. Something very specific has to happen in order to make you death rage, and providing no one plans on using it against you, it's something you can prepare for and avoid. You can stop hanging around those vampires for a while.<br /> <br /> Common is something you can avoid as well, but it's going to inconvenience you. There's no way to predict whether you'll witness a supernatural creature doing something unless you avoid all supernaturals. <br /> <br /> You should probably be putting your problems with the system in the errata thread, so they'll know what they should clean up. It sounds like having it overlap is fine, where you're triggered by specifics and commons at certain harmony, and all of them at the extremes. But it's supposed to be a personal thing and up to the ST to take advantage of it or not, no matter how uncommon or rare you think something is, the Storyteller is the final arbiter of that, and they could just as easily make Luna hang in the sky of the Shadow under the same auspice every night for a month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-14-2015, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T02:37:44-07:00","id":441121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=440443#post440443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's how I understand it as well. What I was saying wouldn't make sense is if you could select them individually, as it has been suggested by a few folks. As in one Passive from any list, one common from any list, and one specific from any list. It would be very strange if your character went from raging any time one of your packmates was injured at 0 or 10, to when you see a Vampire using blood sorcery at 1-2 or 8-9, to when you hear a wolf howl at your auspice moon at 3-4 or 6-7.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And this why I'm plan to House Rule in that with rise of Primal Urge, players choose <b>next</b> Personal Triggers list - so they would have all Moon Triggers, then Blood, etc. Not &quot;one this, one that&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T04:05:24-07:00","id":441180,"title":"","content":"I think the reason for mixing and matching triggers is that the passive ones can render the common and specific obsolete. If you go Moon Moon Moon then while the passive is active you'll rage whenever the moon is in the sky, which means that the more specific ones will never happen because they both require your moon to be in the sky, and you're already raging. It also means you'll only get triggered at certain times of the month.<br /> <br /> By mixing it up you add some variety. You rage no matter what under the full moon, but getting hit with a supernatural power whenever will set you off, as will tasting human blood. For Example.<br /> <br /> I mean, no offence Wyrdhamster but I'm pretty sure what you're suggesting will just result in 24 hour Kuruth party at high primal urge. It's too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":".  typo 03-14-2015, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T04:53:49-07:00","id":441204,"title":"","content":"Yeah,I also thought they were additive so taking the three of them from the same list would be cheating. Say I have:<br /> <br /> <b>Passive:</b> Territory (werewolf you don\u2019t know enters your territory without permission)<br /> <br /> <b>Common:</b> Moon (You witness your auspice moon in the sky)<br /> <br /> <b>Specific:</b> Blood (Swallowing human blood)<br /> <br /> So if I'm balanced I only risk Kuruth when I taste human blood. If I grow imbalanced I risk Kuruth both when tasting human blood and <i>also</i> wen seeing my Auspice Moon on the sky. At worst I would risk Kuruth if I taste human blood <i>or</i> see my auspice's moon <i>or</i> even if my territory is entered by an uninvited werwolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T06:32:58-07:00","id":441248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=441204#post441204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Passive:</b> Territory (werewolf you don\u2019t know enters your territory without permission)<br /> <br /> <b>Common:</b> Moon (You witness your auspice moon in the sky)<br /> <br /> <b>Specific:</b> Blood (Swallowing human blood)</div> </div> </div> </div>You only choose one. Territory OR Moon OR Blood (for example).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T07:03:44-07:00","id":441258,"title":"","content":"I know at least one of the devs has said otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T09:08:05-07:00","id":441396,"title":"","content":"Yes, Acrozatarim allows picking three from three different groups.<br /> <br /> There's no reason triggers have to work on an escalating scale. It's a supernatural thing, and probably tied with some deep psychological stuff. A person may only rage when they taste blood because it calls on some time they were beaten until they choked on their own blood, while someone who's very territorial or xenophobic might freak out if they see another supernatural doing something inhuman and another might react to their auspice moon in the sky because they're very close to their auspice. Or one person might have all those issues and just be able to deal with them better when they're in balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T17:28:37-07:00","id":442005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=441258#post441258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know at least one of the devs has said otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=441396#post441396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Acrozatarim allows picking three from three different groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>He said he was mistaken and that was from an earlier draft.<br /> <br /> <b>You pick one category.</b><br /> Your harmony determines which triggers within that category you use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T17:48:58-07:00","id":442012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433833-some-new-kuruth-triggers#post433833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here's a little something to help fill out the Death Rage Trigger list. These are <i>not</i> official and have <i>not</i> been playtested as yet. Also note that I favour having players pick each Trigger (Passive, Common and Specific) freely from any list they want rather than picking one list and automatically getting all three Triggers from it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The rules don't say either way, we were just going by what Acrozatarim allows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T18:57:32-07:00","id":442078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=441396#post441396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason triggers have to work on an escalating scale. It's a supernatural thing, and probably tied with some deep psychological stuff. A person may only rage when they taste blood because it calls on some time they were beaten until they choked on their own blood, while someone who's very territorial or xenophobic might freak out if they see another supernatural doing something inhuman and another might react to their auspice moon in the sky because they're very close to their auspice. Or one person might have all those issues and just be able to deal with them better when they're in balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest reason is that it makes <i>no sense.</i> Moving smoothly from specific, to common, to passive is a natural and thematic process as your harmony gets increasingly out of balance. Spontaneously developing triggers with no prior thematic connection is somewhat moon moon. It also encourages a lot more min-maxing than picking a category and sticking with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T19:57:39-07:00","id":442110,"title":"","content":"I play a Full Moon. I want my Harmony 10 and Harmony 0 Triggers to be 'the full moon rises'.<br /> <br /> I want to risk Kuruth more often, however, so I take non-Moon triggers for Common and Specific and fit them to my personality. <br /> <br /> I find this fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T21:08:29-07:00","id":442155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442110#post442110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I play a Full Moon. I want my Harmony 10 and Harmony 0 Triggers to be 'the full moon rises'.<br /> I want to risk Kuruth more often, however, so I take non-Moon triggers for Common and Specific and fit them to my personality.<br /> I find this fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can choose to go into Death Rage whenever you want. So you can still go into Death Rage whenever you think it might fit your personality best, in addition your theme triggers and general triggers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T21:20:24-07:00","id":442163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442155#post442155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can choose to go into Death Rage whenever you want. So you can still go into Death Rage whenever you think it might fit your personality best, in addition your theme triggers and general triggers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said I want to risk it, not that I want to intentionally go into it. That is a very different thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T21:42:42-07:00","id":442175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442163#post442163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said I want to risk it, not that I want to intentionally go into it. That is a very different thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every trigger is either something you choose to happen (eating people) or your storyteller makes happen.<br /> I suppose you could roll a die if you wanted risk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T22:08:30-07:00","id":442183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442175#post442175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every trigger is either something you choose to happen (eating people) or your storyteller makes happen.<br /> I suppose you could roll a die if you wanted risk?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, I can just pick and choose my trigger from the lists, which is what I've been getting at the entire time here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T22:12:25-07:00","id":442187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442183#post442183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or, I can just pick and choose my trigger from the lists, which is what I've been getting at the entire time here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aiden, save us all some time and stop returning the volleys. Your opinion is now known, as is Charles Red's. Entertaining this line of conversation further is a waste of energy for everyone and I <i>know</i> y'all don't have the Primal Urge to justify going on like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T22:44:44-07:00","id":442216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442187#post442187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aiden, save us all some time and stop returning the volleys. Your opinion is now known, as is Charles Red's. Entertaining this line of conversation further is a waste of energy for everyone and I <i>know</i> y'all don't have the Primal Urge to justify going on like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is entirely true. I respectfully wish you all the best, Aiden!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T05:55:38-07:00","id":442435,"title":"","content":"When I started this thread, I basically had two questions: &quot;How many triggers does a werewolf have&quot; and &quot;how do you pick them&quot;. <br /> Most things cited (namely Chris' post of new triggers) and the general consensus both seem to point to the answer to the first question being &quot;one at each tier&quot;.<br /> My reading of Chris' post is that he is all for mixing and matching from different lists, but despite his being one of the writers, this was an unofficial stance.<br /> <br /> I came into this thinking that mixing and matching was madness, but the most compelling thing I've heard on the matter was someone pointing out that its a supernatural and personal thing anyway. It doesn't need to follow our earth logic.<br /> On top of that, the game is built to have exceptions to almost every rule, and the space for these exceptions exists to make the stories you tell interesting. While it makes sense to pick one list and run with it so that your character has one highly thematic death rage trigger, I can't honestly think of a reason why actually new triggers couldn't apply as your Uratha gets more and more out of whack. If you want to, as Aiden put it, risk raging more often by not having your specific and common triggers subsumed as your harmony erodes, that's your perogative.<br /> <br /> So I guess the answer to my question of &quot;how many triggers&quot; is &quot;one of each is more than enough&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyone else, specifically devs or people involved in play tests, want to chime in about the intention of experience of running with the current trigger system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T06:09:32-07:00","id":442449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442110#post442110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I play a Full Moon. I want my Harmony 10 and Harmony 0 Triggers to be 'the full moon rises'.<br /> I want to risk Kuruth more often, however, so I take non-Moon triggers for Common and Specific and fit them to my personality. <br /> I find this fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine most storytellers would let you have extra triggers, in addition to all the moon triggers.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, if we go with the AND approach then a character risks Kuruth several times. Someone with Harmony 0 and moon would go into Kuruth when the moon rises, when he first sees the moon, and every time he hears a wolf howl. That's potentially a whole bunch of Kuruth checks.<br /> <br /> Though that also makes me wonder how often you check for Kuruth. Does having passive moon mean you spend the entire night bouncing between wasu and basu? Or just one trigger per scene? Or one trigger per night?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T06:19:18-07:00","id":442452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442435#post442435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Risk raging more often by not having your specific and common triggers subsumed as your harmony erodes, that's your perogative.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is actually nothing to suggest that your triggers are subsumed. But that heavily depends on how frequently you check for Kuruth, as mentioned in my previous post. If you have Territory, and you are constantly death raging for the entire duration another werewolf is in your territory, then they ARE subsumed. But if you go into rage once when you find out they are in your Territory, once when you actually see them, and once when they challenge you... Then they become complimentary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T08:43:07-07:00","id":442593,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\">Internet</span><br /> <b>Passive:</b> Someone is <i>wrong</i> on the Internet.<br /> <b>Common:</b> You see someone being <i>wrong</i> on the Internet.<br /> <b>Specific:</b> Someone trolls you on the Internet.<br /> <br /> /itt.<br /> <br /> Are you <i>sure</i> we're not all Wolf-Blooded? Would we constitute a pack that follows our grand totem, White Wolf?<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> OK, serious mode before Satchel comes and shouts at me. It all falls down to a matter of preference.<br /> <br /> If one party thinks picking and choosing is fun? Then they're right!<br /> <br /> If another party feels that it breaks their immersion, and therefore say you just have to pick it up wholesale? That's fine too!<br /> <br /> In terms of my own preference, I'd go with having to take the <i>whole</i> thing. That way, I (as the ST) have to just remember a pretty simple progression rather than having the Triggers be logically disjoint. Still, I can see some merit in mix-and-match; Mother-Father Luna isn't sane, and that reflects in her children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". I am embarrassed. 03-15-2015, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T08:48:48-07:00","id":442597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442449#post442449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine most storytellers would let you have extra triggers, in addition to all the moon triggers.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, if we go with the AND approach then a character risks Kuruth several times. Someone with Harmony 0 and moon would go into Kuruth when the moon rises, when he first sees the moon, and every time he hears a wolf howl. That's potentially a whole bunch of Kuruth checks.<br /> <br /> Though that also makes me wonder how often you check for Kuruth. Does having passive moon mean you spend the entire night bouncing between wasu and basu? Or just one trigger per scene? Or one trigger per night?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't actually check for Kuruth any more. Entering Wasu-Im <i>is</i> the &quot;check&quot; for Basu-Im.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T09:44:54-07:00","id":442672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442597#post442597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't actually check for Kuruth any more. Entering Wasu-Im <i>is</i> the &quot;check&quot; for Basu-Im.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry I caused any confusion with my phrasing. I meant <b>'check for Kuruth' </b>as in <b>'check for triggers that will start Kuruth'</b>. For example, if there is no cooldown between when you can check for triggers... then you could easily end up with this situation at Harmony 0:<br /> <br /> <b>Moon:</b> My auspice moon is in the sky? Spend the entire night in 3 second Wasu-Im, 10 minute Basu-Im intervals!<br /> <b>Territory:</b> Strange werewolf in my territory? Spend X amount of time in 3 second Wasu-Im, 10 minute Basu-Im intervals (where X may be minutes, hours, days, or weeks depending on how good the werewolf is hiding and cares to stay in your territory).<br /> <b>The Other:</b> You walked into the Hisil? Spend X amount of time in 3 second Wasu-Im, 10 minute Basu-Im intervals (where X is however long it takes your storyteller to have pity on you)<br /> <br /> So for the sake of sanity, it should probably be no more frequently than &quot;Only check each trigger once per scene&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T09:46:02-07:00","id":442674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442593#post442593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Internet</span><br /> <b>Passive:</b> Someone is <i>wrong</i> on the Internet.<br /> <b>Common:</b> You see someone being <i>wrong</i> on the Internet.<br /> <b>Specific:</b> Someone trolls you on the Internet.<br /> <br /> /itt.<br /> <br /> Are you <i>sure</i> we're not all Wolf-Blooded? Would we constitute a pack that follows our grand totem, White Wolf?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We're a <i>tribe</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T11:47:36-07:00","id":442875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442672#post442672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry I caused any confusion with my phrasing. I meant <b>'check for Kuruth' </b>as in <b>'check for triggers that will start Kuruth'</b>. For example, if there is no cooldown between when you can check for triggers... then you could easily end up with this situation at Harmony 0:<br /> <br /> <b>Moon:</b> My auspice moon is in the sky? Spend the entire night in 3 second Wasu-Im, 10 minute Basu-Im intervals!<br /> <b>Territory:</b> Strange werewolf in my territory? Spend X amount of time in 3 second Wasu-Im, 10 minute Basu-Im intervals (where X may be minutes, hours, days, or weeks depending on how good the werewolf is hiding and cares to stay in your territory).<br /> <b>The Other:</b> You walked into the Hisil? Spend X amount of time in 3 second Wasu-Im, 10 minute Basu-Im intervals (where X is however long it takes your storyteller to have pity on you)<br /> <br /> So for the sake of sanity, it should probably be no more frequently than &amp;quot;Only check each trigger once per scene&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see what you're saying. That kind of thing would work fine with the fade to black option (&quot;you awake the next morning lying naked in the woods&quot;, or &quot;when you return to your senses, the intruder lies dead at your feet&quot; or something similar). But if you do play it out, that could be really obnoxious without some kind of limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:13:55-07:00","id":442925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/440056-trigger-warning-to-each-his-own?p=442875#post442875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I see what you're saying. That kind of thing would work fine with the fade to black option (&quot;you awake the next morning lying naked in the woods&quot;, or &quot;when you return to your senses, the intruder lies dead at your feet&quot; or something similar). But if you do play it out, that could be really obnoxious without some kind of limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is something personally horrifying about having 3 seconds of lucidity every 10 minutes, during an entire night full of terror and rampage. A storyteller could craft a very interesting scene combining Fade to Black with fleeting moments of lucidity throughout the night.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it would be very obnoxious for the rest of the players unless they went along with your Basu-Im for the whole night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T13:42:05-07:00","id":443057,"title":"","content":"I don't think you'd even get the three seconds. If a werewolf hits a trigger in Gauru it's straight to hard rage. <br /> <br /> On the one hand this is kinda punishing, on the other it only happens at 10 and 0, so that's par for the course. You only have this problem if you are <i>spectacularly </i>out of whack. It might even help stabilise you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}